  "answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics and optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility. The project was initially introduced with a kickoff scheduled for mid-June or July 2023, led by Sarah Tan or Marcus Cole, with an initial phase budget of $500,000. The team was later expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding in September. The executive board subsequently approved a total budget of $2 million covering research, development, and marketing, and a separate $15,000 budget was approved for specialized training. Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, with the next phase focusing on user interface enhancements starting in October. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience was requested by the end of November. Security protocols were updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January of the following year. The project is described as almost complete, with contributors and action items acknowledged."
